619f429f9b660506954639/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: bash]\nLet me view all source and tests.\n[tool: bash]\nSix bugs, all clear. Fixing them now.\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\nAll 16 tests pass now. The first run showed 15 because `test_search` couldn't be imported and was counted as one error; it actually contains 2 tests.\n\n**What the three reads returned:**\n- **(a)** Reading the `catalog/` directory listed its 8 entries: `__init__.py`, `books.py`, `factory.py`, `fees.py`, `inventory.py`, `members.py`, `search.py`, `text.py`.\n- **(b)** Offset 0, limit 5 returned lines 1\u20135. An offset of 0 is treated as the start of the file.\n- **(c)** Offset 3, limit 5 returned lines 3\u20137. So the offset is a 1-indexed line number, and the two reads overlapped on lines 3\u20135.\n\n**Fixes (only files in `catalog/` were changed; the tests are untouched):**\n1. `books.py`: `parse_book` left the year as a string. It now uses `int(year)`, which fixed both `test_year_is_int` and the `TypeError` in `age()`.\n2. `factory.py`: the third sample book, `Book(\"Emma\", \"Austen\", 1815, 1)`, was missing. I added it, which also matches the docstring.\n3. `fees.py`: the fee was `days_late + DAILY_FEE` and is now `days_late * DAILY_FEE`.\n4. `inventory.py`: `recent(n)` sliced `[-n - 1:]`, which returned one event too many. It now slices `[-n:]`. I also made `n <= 0` return an empty list, because `[-0:]` would return the whole history.\n5. `members.py`: `MAX_BORROWED` was 3, which contradicted the comment about a five-book policy and the tests. It is now 5.\n6. `search.py`: it imported `normalize` from `catalog.nonexistent`, which doesn't exist. It now imports from `catalog.text`.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 8, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 69010, "requests_cache_write": 64631, "requests_cost_usd": 0.39945299999999995, "requests_count": 6, "requests_input_uncached": 14, "requests_output": 3122, "reread": true, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "opencode:trig-read-edge:claude-opus-5-5:trial18", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 215, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-19T20:26:20.104347+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 33.966, "t_checker_s": 0.176, "t_env_setup_s": 0.002, "task": "trig-read-edge", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "vendor_split", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 3136, "tokens_cache_read": 69010, "tokens_cache_write": 64631, "tokens_fresh": 3136, "tokens_input_uncached": 14, "tokens_main_cache_read": 69010, "tokens_main_cache_write": 64631, "tokens_main_calls": 6, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 14, "tokens_main_output": 3122, "tokens_output": 3122, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 69010, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": 64631, "tokens_proxy_calls": 6, "tokens_proxy_input_uncached": 14, "tokens_proxy_output": 3122, "tokens_proxy_reasoning": null, "tokens_reasoning": 0, "toolchain": {"ai": "6.0.168", "anthropic": "3.0.64", "bun": "1.3.13"}, "trial": 18, "ts_iso": "2026-10-19T16:26:21", "turn_mode": null, "turns": 6, "upstream_model": "claude-opus-5-5", "usage_raw": [{"cache": {"read": 0, "write": 15317}, "input": 4, "output": 516, "reasoning": 0, "total": 15837}, {"cache": {"read":